  "stem": "What is the greatest solution to the equation \\(\\sqrt{5x + 1} = x + 1\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "3"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Square both sides: \\(5x + 1 = x^{2} + 2x + 1\\).",
    "Rearrange: \\(x^{2} - 3x = 0\\), so \\(x(x - 3) = 0\\) and \\(x = 0\\) or \\(x = 3\\).",
    "Check both in the original equation: \\(\\sqrt{1} = 1 = 0 + 1\\) and \\(\\sqrt{16} = 4 = 3 + 1\\). Neither is extraneous, so the greatest solution is \\(3\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nsols = solve(Eq(sqrt(5*x + 1), x + 1), x)\nassert sorted(sols) == [0, 3]\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == max(sols) == 3",
